-- A `=>`-constrained wrapper whose body is an under-applied constrained callee
-- (`trav identity`, trav needing one more arg), dict-passed through clause
-- `[$dict]`.  The emitter formerly gave the wrapper's define arity 1 (dict only)
-- while the saturated call site passed dict + the list → the value arg was
-- dropped and the inner trav ran on garbage → SIGSEGV at runtime (native `run`
-- was correct; only build+exec crashed).  Fixed by extending methodBodyDeficit
-- to eta-saturate an under-applied CDict-spine body (llvm_emit.mdk).
--
-- The wrapper was originally the point-free `seqp = trav identity`.  That shape
-- is now rejected at the definition (T-SIG-OVER-EXPANSIVE — a polymorphic
-- signature over an expansive body; HM-CORE-SEMANTICS §1 clause 4), so the
-- fixture carries the eta-expanded form and pins the dispatch, not the deficit.
--
-- GOLDEN IS NATIVE-SOURCED (native>oracle): the frozen OCaml oracle mis-evaluates
-- this shape (returns `[[1, 2, 3]]`); the .build.golden is captured from the native
-- `medaka build`+exec, which matches native `run`.
trav : Thenable m => (a -> m b) -> List a -> m (List b)
trav f xs = match xs
  []        => pure []
  (x::rest) => andThen (f x) (y => andThen (trav f rest) (ys => pure (y :: ys)))

seqp : Thenable m => List (m a) -> m (List a)
seqp xs = trav identity xs

main : <IO> Unit
main = println (debug (seqp [Some 1, Some 2, Some 3]))
